# C# Backend

Conventions and boundaries live in `AGENTS.md` (hard rules); the wire contract lives in the
`asher-jsonl-protocol` skill. Apply those when editing C#.

Cursor-specific:

- `Asher.Host` stdout is JSONL protocol only; diagnostics go to stderr.
- Contracts are DTO-oriented (`Asher.Services/Application/Contracts/`); do not expose internal
  service types on the wire.
- Backend projects must not reference Electron, WPF, or Prism.
- Build: `dotnet build <project>.csproj -c Debug -p:Platform=x86` (Windows); Linux builds are
  AnyCPU/x64. Full commands: `asher-testing` skill.
